# KPI Plus UI — Design Spec A

- Source of truth: `docs/design/DESIGN-SPEC-A.md`
- Dashboard home (`/crm`) uses presentation tokens `--kpi-a-*` only — no raw hex in components
- Text on brand lime (`#A2DC25`) must be `#1A3A02`, never white
- Minimum readable text size: 13px; dashboard base 17px (16px on small screens)
- KPI / summary numbers: `font-weight: 700` + `font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`
- Warning colors (rose/amber) only when the value is greater than 0
- Do not invent modules or routes; filter by existing `hasModule` / permissions
- Do not change backend, Prisma schema, or API contracts when restyling
- Prefer Prompt for dashboard chrome; keep public-site CI typography (Montserrat / Sarabun) on marketing pages
- Keep CrmShell as the only app sidebar — do not nest a second sidebar on the dashboard
- Component files under `web/components/crm/dashboard/` stay under ~200 lines each
